0 -18 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(The Bag-of-Words \(BoW\) model represents text by measuring word occurrences while) Tj
0 -14 Td
(discarding grammar, word order, and syntax. A text document is converted into a) Tj
0 -14 Td
(numeric sparse vector where each dimension corresponds to a specific vocabulary) Tj
0 -14 Td
(term and the scalar value denotes term frequency.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(While intuitive and effective for basic document categorization, the Bag-of-Words) Tj
0 -14 Td
(model suffers from high vector dimensionality, extreme sparsity, and complete) Tj
0 -14 Td
(blindness to semantic synonymy.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 12 Tf
(5.2 TF-IDF Formulation) Tj
0 -18 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency \(TF-IDF\) is a statistical weighting) Tj
0 -14 Td
(metric that evaluates how important a word is to a document within a larger) Tj
0 -14 Td
(collection or corpus of documents.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Term Frequency \(TF\) measures the frequency of word t within document d: TF\(t, d\) =) Tj
0 -14 Td
(count\(t, d\) / total_words\(d\). Common variations apply logarithmic smoothing: TF\(t,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(d\) = 1 + log\(count\(t, d\)\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Inverse Document Frequency \(IDF\) penalizes words that appear across virtually all) Tj
0 -14 Td
(documents in the corpus, assigning higher importance to rare, discriminative) Tj
0 -14 Td
(terms:) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(-  IDF\(t, D\) = log\( \(1 + Total_Documents\) / \(1 + Documents_Containing\(t\)\) \) + 1) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -4 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(The compound TF-IDF score is the product: TF-IDF\(t, d, D\) = TF\(t, d\) * IDF\(t, D\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Words with high TF-IDF scores have high frequency in a specific document but low) Tj
0 -14 Td
(frequency across the wider corpus, making them effective keywords for information) Tj
0 -14 Td
(retrieval and document indexing.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 12 Tf
