(8. The Attention Mechanism and Context Alignment) Tj
0 -24 Td
/F1 12 Tf
(8.1 The Information Bottleneck in Encoder-Decoder Models) Tj
0 -18 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Traditional sequence-to-sequence \(Seq2Seq\) architectures use an RNN encoder to) Tj
0 -14 Td
(compress an entire input sequence into a single fixed-length context vector before) Tj
0 -14 Td
(decoding. This creates a severe information bottleneck: as input sentences grow) Tj
0 -14 Td
(longer \(exceeding 20-30 tokens\), the fixed vector cannot retain all salient) Tj
0 -14 Td
(details, causing translation accuracy to deteriorate sharply.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 12 Tf
(8.2 Bahdanau Additive Attention) Tj
0 -18 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(The attention mechanism \(Bahdanau et al., 2014\) eliminated the fixed vector) Tj
0 -14 Td
(bottleneck by allowing the decoder to dynamically attend to all encoder hidden) Tj
0 -14 Td
(states at every decoding step.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Instead of relying on a single vector, the decoder computes alignment energy) Tj
0 -14 Td
(scores between the current decoder state and all encoder hidden states, normalizes) Tj
0 -14 Td
(them via softmax into attention weights, and computes a dynamic context vector as) Tj
0 -14 Td
(a weighted sum of encoder representations.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 12 Tf
(8.3 Scaled Dot-Product Attention) Tj
0 -18 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Vaswani et al. \(2017\) formalized attention as a mapping from a Query vector and a) Tj
0 -14 Td
(set of Key-Value vector pairs to an output vector. Scaled Dot-Product Attention is) Tj
0 -14 Td
(formulated as:) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(-  Attention\(Q, K, V\) = Softmax\( \(Q * K^T\) / sqrt\(d_k\) \) * V) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -4 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Where Q represents Queries \(dimension d_k\), K represents Keys, and V represents) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Values. The scaling factor 1 / sqrt\(d_k\) prevents the dot products from growing) Tj
0 -14 Td
(excessively large for large dimensions, which would otherwise push the softmax) Tj
0 -14 Td
(function into regions with vanishingly small gradients.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 12 Tf
(8.4 Self-Attention) Tj
0 -18 Td
/F1 10 Tf
